# @toolofna/pitchcraft-chrome — environment variables it reads
#
# Chrome is a library: the *deck* owns its real .env.local. This file
# documents the variables chrome's server entry points read so a deck (or
# the factory) sets them correctly. Copy the relevant lines into the
# deck's .env.local / Railway service variables.

# ─── Auth (NextAuth / Auth.js v5) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Generate AUTH_SECRET with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
AUTH_SECRET=
# Google OAuth — Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=

# ─── Team-identity gate (SECURITY — set for production) ────────────────
# Comma-separated emails that are deck OWNERS — the high-trust allowlist
# for curation, queue dispatch, accent, structural slide ops, and PUSH.
#
# REQUIRED in production. If this is EMPTY, NO ONE can curate/publish via
# the owner path — chrome will NOT fall open to a self-assigned "creative"
# role (that was a privilege-escalation bug). Team members can still be
# granted privileges without being listed here ONLY if they sign in with a
# verified toolofna.com Google account (hosted-domain verified server-side
# from the Google `hd` + `email_verified` claims). External clients can
# always sign in and comment as `client`; they can never self-assign a
# team role.
#
# So: list at least the deck owner here for production, or rely on
# verified toolofna.com sign-in. Empty + non-team accounts = deny.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DECK_OWNER_EMAILS=

# ─── Deck URL (SECURITY — used for trusted Slack links) ────────────────
# The deck's public base URL. Used to build the "Open in deck" link in
# Slack notifications. Server-trusted: chrome prefers this over the
# request Host / X-Forwarded-* headers (which are attacker-controllable)
# so a link in a trusted internal Slack DM can't be pointed elsewhere.
# The factory sets one of these per deck (e.g. https://<slug>.toolofna.dev).
# Falls back to request headers only for local dev when all are unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DECK_URL=
# AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# NEXTAUTH_URL=

# ─── Persistence ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Redis connection string (Railway managed Redis). When unset, chrome
# falls back to an in-process memory store (local dev only).
REDIS_URL=

# ─── Slack notifications (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# Bot scopes: chat:write, users:read, users:read.email
# Leave SLACK_BOT_TOKEN blank to disable Slack notifications entirely.
# SLACK_CHANNEL blank = DM mode (default); set = post to that channel.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
SLACK_CHANNEL=

# ─── Send-to-Claude dispatch (per-deck) ────────────────────────────────
# PAT/GitHub App token with issues:write on the deck repo, and the repo
# in owner/name form. Required for the queue → Claude triage flow.
GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN=
PITCHCRAFT_GH_REPO=
